7. Experimental Framework

7.1 Datasets and Tasks

· Question Answering: TruthfulQA (hallucination sensitivity), Natural Questions (knowledge-intensive).
· Multi-Step Reasoning: GSM8K (math), StrategyQA (implicit reasoning).
· Code Generation: HumanEval, MBPP.
· Agentic Tasks: WebShop (simulated e-commerce), API-Bank (tool-augmented).
· Agentic Hallucination: MIRAGE-Bench (full taxonomy).

7.2 Baselines

· Single-pass LLM (Llama-3-70B-Instruct / GPT-4o-mini as Fast Path).
· Static Multi-Agent Pipeline: Always runs reasoning + retrieval + verification.
· CGR / Entropy-Based Stopping: Representative single-model adaptive baselines.
· SOFAI-LLM: The two-solver meta-cognitive baseline (fast LLM + slow LRM).
· ACB (Full): Complete architecture.

7.3 Metrics

· Accuracy: Task-specific (exact match, F1).
· Token Consumption: Sum of all model input/output tokens per query.
· Latency: End-to-end wall-clock time, with TTFT < 500 ms and total < 4 s annotated using HCI responsiveness standards.
· Energy: Estimated via EcoLogits methodology: tokens → kWh using hardware-specific coefficients, then → gCO₂e via regional carbon intensity.
· Calibration Quality: ECE, Brier Score, Selective AUROC, and conformal conditional coverage \mathbb{P}(\text{correct} \mid C \geq \tau_\alpha).
· Hallucination Rate: FActScore (extrinsic), SelfCheckGPT score (intrinsic), MIRAGE-Bench (agentic).
· Budget Compliance: Percentage of queries exceeding B_{\max}.
· Pareto Hypervolume: Area under the accuracy–cost frontier.

7.4 Falsifiable Hypotheses

H1 (Efficiency): ACB reduces total token consumption by at least 30% compared to the static multi-agent pipeline on mixed-difficulty benchmarks, while maintaining accuracy within 2% of the static baseline.

H2 (Hallucination Reduction): ACB's selective verification yields a lower hallucination rate (MIRAGE-Bench) than single-pass generation and consumes fewer tokens than an always-on verification baseline.

H2a (Extrinsic vs. Intrinsic): ACB reduces extrinsic hallucination (H_{\text{ext}}) by ≥40% relative to single-pass, with ≤15% token overhead vs. no-verification, and reduces H_{\text{ext}} more than H_{\text{int}} because retrieval specifically addresses missing knowledge.

H3 (Pareto Dominance): In the accuracy–efficiency trade-off space, ACB lies closer to the Pareto frontier than both the static pipeline and single-model adaptive baselines, as measured by hypervolume under the frontier.

7.5 Ablation Study

Five configurations tested on 500 queries stratified by difficulty (easy/medium/hard):

· ACB-Full: Complete architecture.
· ACB-NoConf: Replace the IB-EDL conformal confidence estimator with random scores (uniform [0,1]).
· ACB-NoGate: Remove the Decision Gate; always escalate to the full agent pipeline.
· ACB-NoVerify: Omit the verification agent; confidence relies solely on token entropy and self-consistency.
· Static-Baseline: Always-on multi-agent pipeline (reasoning + retrieval + verification).

7.6 Human-Centric Pilot

A pilot study with N = 20 participants on a customer-support task measures:

· Interaction steps to resolution (proxy for cognitive load).
· User satisfaction via 5-point Likert scale and the CASUX instrument for conversational agent UX.
· Goal momentum score following the PULSE framework, using a lightweight classifier trained on behavioral features to predict user satisfaction.

We note these metrics are exploratory and call for standardized agent UX benchmarks in future work.

7.7 Gate Training Protocol

The gate is bootstrapped using off-policy bandit learning:

1. Critic training: The IB-EDL critic is trained on the adversarial calibration set (CCPS-style perturbations on confidently-wrong queries), plus standard calibration data.
2. Conformal calibration: Split the calibration set; compute conformal threshold \tau_\alpha for desired risk level \alpha = 0.05.
3. Policy training: Collect trajectories from static pipelines and initial ACB with uniform random exploration. Compute post-hoc rewards using VoC and train the LinUCB or PPO policy offline on logged data.
4. Final evaluation: Held-out tasks with greedy policy.

