Appendix H: Evaluation Metrics Definitions

H.1 Calibration Metrics

Expected Calibration Error (ECE). Partition the probability space into M bins B_m. For each bin, compute \text{acc}(B_m) = fraction of correct answers among predictions with confidence in that bin, and \text{conf}(B_m) = average confidence in that bin. Then:

\text{ECE} = \sum_{m=1}^{M} \frac{|B_m|}{N} \left| \text{acc}(B_m) - \text{conf}(B_m) \right|.

Brier Score. \[\text{Brier} = \frac{1}{N} \sum_{i=1}^{N} (C_i - \omega_i)^2,\] where \omega_i = 1 if answer correct, else 0.

Selective AUROC. The area under the ROC curve for predicting correctness from the confidence score. Higher values indicate better separation.

Conformal Conditional Coverage. \[\text{Coverage}(\alpha) = \frac{1}{N_{\text{test}}} \sum_{i=1}^{N_{\text{test}}} \mathbf{1}[C_i \ge 1-\tau_\alpha \land \omega_i = 1] / \mathbf{1}[C_i \ge 1-\tau_\alpha].\] Should be \ge 1-\alpha.

H.2 Hallucination Metrics

FActScore (Extrinsic). Decompose answer into atomic facts. For each fact, check if supported by a trusted knowledge source. H_{\text{ext}} = (# unsupported facts) / (# total facts).

SelfCheckGPT (Intrinsic). Sample multiple answers. For each sentence, compute the average semantic similarity to other samples; low similarity indicates hallucination. Overall score H_{\text{int}} is the aggregate across sentences.

MIRAGE-Bench Score. Fine-grained LLM-as-a-judge scoring along three axes: instruction faithfulness, history faithfulness, environment faithfulness. Reported as mean scores.

H.3 Pareto Hypervolume

The Pareto frontier is the set of non-dominated (accuracy, cost) points. Hypervolume is the area under the frontier up to a reference point (e.g., (0, max cost)). Larger hypervolume indicates a better trade-off.

