Appendix I: Additional Related Work (Expanded)

I.1 Cognitive Science Foundations

The resource-rational analysis framework (Gershman et al., 2015; Lieder & Griffiths, 2020) has been applied to human decision-making, planning, and metacognition. ACB draws direct inspiration from the notion that humans allocate cognitive resources based on the expected value of computation. The VoC formulation is a realization of this principle in artificial systems.

I.2 Speculative Cascades and Bidirectional Routing

Speculative cascades (Chen et al., 2025) combine a fast drafter model with a larger verifier, improving latency by parallel execution. ACB’s cascaded confidence gating is analogous but applies to heterogeneous orchestration decisions rather than sequential token generation.

I.3 Agentic Hallucination Benchmarks

MIRAGE-Bench (Zhang et al., 2025) is the first comprehensive benchmark for hallucinations in interactive LLM agents. It includes tasks that test consistency with instructions, history, and environment. ACB’s verification agent uses a similar detection pipeline.

I.4 Energy Profiling for LLMs

The Cost of Dynamic Reasoning (2025) provides system-level energy traces. EcoLogits offers per-query CO₂e estimation. ACB adopts these tools for its evaluation.

