1. Introduction

1.1 Purpose

This document defines the technical specification for the Adaptive Cognitive Budgeting (ACB) system, a meta‑cognitive orchestration layer for large language model (LLM) agent systems. ACB dynamically allocates inference compute across a heterogeneous capability stack—single‑pass generation, chain‑of‑thought reasoning, retrieval‑augmented generation (RAG), agent delegation, and fact‑verification—based on confidence, epistemic uncertainty, task utility, and remaining computational budget.

1.2 Scope

The specification covers:

· System architecture and component decomposition
· Mathematical models for confidence, uncertainty, decision‑theoretic gating, and budget optimisation
· Detailed algorithms and pseudocode
· Data flow, interfaces, and API definitions
· Deployment architecture on vLLM‑based infrastructure
· Configuration parameters and performance metrics

Out of scope for this document:

· Detailed training procedures for the IB‑EDL critic and bandit policy (see separate training guide)
· Hardware‑specific provisioning details

1.3 Definitions & Abbreviations

