3. Architectural Design

3.1 Layered Architecture

```
┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐
│   L1: Fast Inference                     │
├──────────────────────────────────────────┤
│   L2: Cascaded Confidence Estimation     │
├──────────────────────────────────────────┤
│   L3: Meta‑Cognitive Control (Gate)      │
├──────────────────────────────────────────┤
│   L4: Capability Execution               │
├──────────────────────────────────────────┤
│   L5: Verification & Budget Tracking     │
└──────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

Each layer is an independent, replaceable microservice. Communication is via synchronous gRPC with protobuf message schemas.

3.2 Component Diagram

```
Query --> [Fast‑Path LLM] --> (y0, logprobs) --> [Confidence Estimator (cascade)]
        │
        └──> [IB‑EDL Critic] ──> (C, u) ──> [Conformal Threshold Check]
                                                    │
                                          ┌────────┴─────────┐
                                          │  Decision Gate   │
                                          │  (Bandit Policy) │
                                          └────────┬─────────┘
                              ┌───────────────────┼───────────────────┐
                              ▼                   ▼                   ▼
                        [Refine (CoT)]      [Retrieve (RAG)]   [Agent Delegation]
                              │                   │                   │
                              └───────────────────┼───────────────────┘
                                                  ▼
                                          [Verification Agent]
                                                  │
                                              (Answer + cost)
```

All components are stateless except the Decision Gate, which maintains per‑query state in a short‑lived session cache.

