8. Deployment Architecture

8.1 Infrastructure

· Orchestration: vLLM 0.6.0+ with WRP (Workload‑Router‑Pool) plugin.
· Model serving: separate vLLM instances for fast‑path (8B), reasoning (70B), critic (shared 8B trunk + heads).
· Vector DB: Milvus for retrieval index (≥ 10M documents).
· Message bus: Kafka topic acb/queries for logging and offline training.

8.2 WRP Integration

· Workload (W): client‑side agent versus simple chat.
· Router (R): ACB Decision Gate as a “semantic router” plugin; receives features from vLLM request scheduler.
· Pool (P): GPU groups: pool‑fast (T4/A10G), pool‑heavy (A100‑80GB), pool‑retrieval (CPU offload with GPU reader).

8.3 Lagrangian Soft‑Budget Controller

· Dual variable \lambda updated periodically via cloud watch metrics.
· GitOps config map: budget_target: 2000 tokens/query.
· Implemented as sidecar to the gate.

8.4 Scaling

· Horizontal scaling: gate is stateless per request (session cache with TTL).
· Confidence estimator: critic model replicated with load balancer.
· Capability executors: auto‑scale based on queue depth.

